      "message": "system_get_fw_reset_vector is a chip defined function, not a board defined function.\n\nLooking at system_run_image_copy_with_flags(), we may want to convert this to a Kconfig choice.\n\nchoice PLATFORM_EC_SYSJUMP_TYPE\n     default PLATFORM_EC_SYSJUMP_BOOTROM if PLATFORM_EC_EXTERNAL_STORAGE\n     default PLATFORM_EC_SYSJUMP_CHIP_DEFINED if SOC_FAMILY_RISCV_ITE\n     default PLATFORM_EC_SYSJUMP_ARM\n \nPLATFORM_EC_SYSJUMP_BOOTROM: Chip bootrom code used for sysjump. Required for ECs that execute code in RAM.\nPLATFORM_EC_SYSJUMP_CHIP_DEFINED: Chip defined reset vector\nPLATFORM_EC_SYSJUMP_ARM: Standard ARM reset vector (reset vector address expected to be located at 4 byte offset into the image).\n\nThis would require renaming CONFIG_FW_RESET_VECTOR to CONFIG_SYSJUMP_CHIP_DEFINED.  And a minor refactor of system_run_image_copy_with_flags() to use the new config names.",
